{% assign cf = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values %}
{% assign band = cf.band %}
{% assign mode = cf.mode %}
{% unless mode %}
  {% if spots.size > 0 %}{% assign mode = spots[0].mode | downcase %}{% else %}{% assign mode = 'all' %}{% endif %}
{% endunless %}
{% unless band %}
  {% assign band = 'all' %}
  {% for c in counts %}
    {% if forloop.first and forloop.last %}{% assign band = c[0] %}{% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
{% endunless %}
{% assign icon_svg = '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="black" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M2 9 C5 3, 9 3, 12 9 C15 15, 19 15, 22 9"/><path d="M2 15 C5 9, 9 9, 12 15 C15 21, 19 21, 22 15"/></svg>' %}

{% comment %}
the map svg scales freely to fill the view at any device or slot size. the
positioned wrapper is sized in container-query units (100cqw x 100cqh, which
measure the actual layout container even inside mashup slots) so the svg and
mask always have a definite box -- percentage heights alone fail to resolve in
shallow mashup slots and let the svg overflow. the svg letterboxes its content
into that box via xMidYMid meet, fitting both bounds.
land shading is composited separately: the absolutely-positioned div carries
the framework bg--gray-60 class in screen space -- so its pattern is always
pixel-perfect -- and a css mask (data-uri svg of the land path, same viewBox
and default meet as the map svg) clips it to the continents. both svgs
letterbox identically, so the layers stay aligned at any size. inline styles
here are limited to positioning, sizing, and masking, which the framework has
no utilities for.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="layout layout--col layout--stretch">
  <div class="flex flex--center stretch-x stretch-y">
    <div style="position:relative;width:100cqw;height:100cqh">
      <div class="bg--gray-60" style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;-webkit-mask-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,{{ world_mask_b64 }}');-webkit-mask-size:100% 100%;mask-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,{{ world_mask_b64 }}');mask-size:100% 100%"></div>
      <svg width="100%" height="100%" viewBox="0 0 720 360" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" style="position:relative">
        {% for s in spots %}
        <path d="{{ s.path }}" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        {% endfor %}
        {% for s in spots %}
        <circle cx="{{ s.x1 }}" cy="{{ s.y1 }}" r="2.6" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        {% endfor %}
        {% for s in spots %}
        <circle cx="{{ s.x2 }}" cy="{{ s.y2 }}" r="2.6" fill="#000000" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width="1"/>
        {% endfor %}
        {% if spots.size == 0 %}
        <rect x="180" y="164" width="360" height="32" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#000000"/>
        <text x="360" y="184" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#000000">no spots heard in the last 6 hours</text>
        {% endif %}
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="title_bar">
  <img class="image" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,{{ icon_svg | base64_encode }}" />
  <span class="title">RBN Map</span>
  <span class="instance">{% if mode == 'all' %}all modes{% else %}{{ mode | upcase }}{% endif %} &middot; {% if band == 'all' %}all bands{% else %}{{ band }}{% endif %}{% if cf.dx_call and cf.dx_call != '' %} &middot; dx {{ cf.dx_call | strip | upcase }}{% endif %}{% if cf.de_call and cf.de_call != '' %} &middot; de {{ cf.de_call | strip | upcase }}{% endif %} &middot; {{ spots.size }} spot{% unless spots.size == 1 %}s{% endunless %}</span>
</div>
